{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJ8AwNsY8Job7N7kcM3zod","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel01.1\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel01.1 — cat specification and differential test\"\n     3→release: rel01.1\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel01.1-uc001-cat\n     7→  - prd006-cat R1\n     8→  - prd006-cat R2\n     9→  - prd006-cat R3\n    10→  - prd006-cat R4\n    11→  - prd006-cat R5\n    12→\n    13→preconditions:\n    14→  - ./bin/cat exists (built via mage build).\n    15→  - Reference binary gcat is installed via Homebrew (coreutils) and on PATH.\n    16→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/cat/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    17→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    18→  - \"cat: no normalization is applied; cat output is deterministic. Binary test inputs are specified as hex escape sequences.\"\n    19→\n    20→test_cases:\n    21→  - name: cat_default_passthrough\n    22→    description: 'No flags, text file content passes through verbatim. Setup: file1.txt contains \"hello\\nworld\\n\"'\n    23→    inputs:\n    24→      args: [\"file1.txt\"]\n    25→      stdin: null\n    26→      env: []\n    27→    normalization: none\n    28→    expected:\n    29→      exit_code: 0\n    30→      stdout: \"hello\\nworld\\n\"\n    31→      stderr: \"\"\n    32→    traces:\n    33→      - prd006-cat R1.1\n    34→      - prd006-cat R1.5\n    35→\n    36→  - name: cat_binary_passthrough\n    37→    description: No flags, binary input (all byte values 0x00-0xFF) passes through without corruption.\n    38→    inputs:\n    39→      args: []\n    40→      stdin: \"\\\\x00\\\\x01\\\\x02...\\\\xfe\\\\xff (all 256 byte values)\"\n    41→      env: []\n    42→    normalization: none\n    43→    expected:\n    44→      exit_code: 0\n    45→      stdout: identical 256 bytes as input\n    46→      stderr: \"\"\n    47→    traces:\n    48→      - prd006-cat R1.4\n    49→\n 